id: pm-brief-javk
title: Alert on daily release failure and require merge drivers in CI
description: "Two CI fixes: (1) release.yml gets an if:failure() job that opens or updates one deduplicated tracking issue (label release-failure, stable title) with job name, run URL, commit SHA and date; issues:write only, never blocks a release. (2) ci.yml installs pm merge drivers before the health gate and passes --require-merge-drivers so a fresh clone without clone-local driver config fails the gate instead of silently passing. Motivated by five unnoticed failed daily releases (2026-08-17..2026-08-22) caused by an expired npm token."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-22T18:44:47.348Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-24T08:36:24.529Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-22T18:47:50.012Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-22T18:47:50.012Z"
claim_principal: ox-alpha
author: ox-alpha
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-24T08:36:24.529Z",pi-agent,"CodeRabbit PR #79 thread 3836774695 resolved with real evidence instead of a live release run: the alert step's inline script was extracted verbatim into scripts/alert-on-release-failure.sh and the workflow job now checks out the repo and runs it, so workflow and tests execute the same bytes. New hermetic suite test/alert-on-release-failure.test.ts stubs gh on PATH and proves all three behaviours the YAML verifier could not: single create with release-failure label + stable title + run URL/commit/date body; comment-on-existing-#77 deduplication without a second create; and exit 0 plus ::warning:: when every gh call fails. Mutation proof: with the dedup lookup broken (existing_number emptied), the suite fails 3/4 tests; restored, 4/4 pass. shellcheck v0.10.0 clean; npm test 274 pass; coverage thresholds met (100 lines/92.15 branches/100 functions); pm health --strict-exit green; changelog:full+check green."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-22T18:44:52.174Z",ox-alpha,"Gate proof: removed all five merge.pm-* config sections, ./node_modules/.bin/pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers exited 1; after ./node_modules/.bin/pm merge install it exited 0. Plain --strict-exit stays 0 both ways."
files[4]:
  - path: .github/workflows/ci.yml
    scope: project
  - path: .github/workflows/release.yml
    scope: project
  - path: scripts/alert-on-release-failure.sh
    scope: project
    note: extracted alert step script; workflow and tests execute the same bytes
  - path: test/alert-on-release-failure.test.ts
    scope: project
    note: "hermetic stub-gh proof of create,dedup comment,and non-blocking warning paths"
tests[6]{command,path,scope,note}:
  git config --local --remove-section merge.pm-item-toon && ./node_modules/.bin/pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers,.,project,health gate exits non-zero when clone-local merge drivers are absent
  python3 .agents/pm/verify-release-yaml.py,.github/workflows/release.yml,project,"release.yml parses as YAML; alert-on-release-failure job has if: failure(), needs: release, permissions issues:write"
  npm test,test/alert-on-release-failure.test.ts,project,"hermetic alert script test: creates the deduplicated release-failure issue with run URL, commit, and date when no open issue exists"
  npm run test,test/alert-on-release-failure.test.ts,project,"hermetic alert script test: comments on the existing open release-failure issue instead of creating a second one"
  npm --silent test,test/alert-on-release-failure.test.ts,project,"hermetic alert script test: stays non-blocking (exit 0) and emits ::warning:: when every gh call fails"
  "npm run build:test && npm test",test/alert-on-release-failure.test.ts,project,"release.yml wiring: the alert job checks out the repository and executes scripts/alert-on-release-failure.sh"
close_reason: "Both fixes implemented, YAML-verified and gate proven (RC 1 without drivers, 0 after pm merge install); npm test 270 pass; release:check green"
body: ""
